{"case_id": "oos-005", "question": "What is sin(30 degrees)?", "out_of_scope_topic": "trigonometry", "out_of_scope_reason": "Trigonometric ratios are not part of the Class 1-5 list (angle MEASUREMENT with a protractor is a Class 5 topic, but trigonometric functions are not).", "boundary_case": true, "boundary_case_note": "Tests whether the system conflates 'this mentions angles/degrees, which IS Class 5 content' with trigonometry, which is not.", "expected_behavior": "Recognize that mentioning degrees does not make this Class 5 angle-measurement content; decline to answer as a trigonometry problem.", "must_avoid": ["Answering '0.5' and treating it as equivalent to a Class 5 angle question because both mention degrees."], "notes": "", "truly_out_of_scope": true, "live_scope_gate_result": {"in_scope": true, "topic": null, "allow_gloss": false}}
{"case_id": "oos-006", "question": "What is the square root of -4?", "out_of_scope_topic": "complex numbers", "out_of_scope_reason": "Complex/imaginary numbers are not part of the Class 1-5 list.", "boundary_case": true, "boundary_case_note": "Tests whether the system attempts a real-number answer, states a wrong real value, or correctly recognises this needs imaginary numbers and declines either way.", "expected_behavior": "Decline to answer; do not state a real-number value as if it were correct, and do not silently assume the student made a typo.", "must_avoid": ["Stating a real number (e.g. claiming the square root of -4 is -2 or undefined-as-an-error rather than acknowledging it needs a concept beyond scope).", "Silently correcting the question to sqrt(4) without telling the student."], "notes": "This item also probes a secondary risk (silent question substitution), not just scope recognition.", "truly_out_of_scope": true, "live_scope_gate_result": {"in_scope": false, "topic": "roots (square/cube root)", "allow_gloss": true}}
